From: quickjs-ng register-VM work
Subject: AOT: Layer A inline fast paths

What this does
  Lowers the hottest register-VM operations directly in the generated unit
  instead of calling the step engine, and shrinks the entry fill using the
  backend's existing definite-assignment analysis.

  Forty ROPs get a template that mirrors its interpreter handler one-for-one:
  property reads (get_field, get_field_own, get_field2, get_field2_own and the
  fused get_field_chain/get_field_chain_own), put_field, get_element,
  get_local/put_local (+short forms), get_arg, get_var_ref, load_this, move,
  move_s, move_xfer, the load_* constants, get_global, the arithmetic and fused
  arithmetic ops, binary_imm, the branches (branch, branch_s, branch_if,
  branch_if_not, branch_cmp_reg_reg + short) and the generic binop/unop
  families. Everything else still falls back to qjs_aot_step. This covers ~92%
  of box2d's dynamic operations.

  The templates reach the engine through a small set of always_inline helpers
  (qjs_aot_num_fast, qjs_aot_own_read_hit, qjs_aot_set_reg_p, ...). They are
  inlined across the translation unit with -flto, which is what brings the
  compiled hot set below the interpreter (3.66G vs 4.92G instructions on
  box2d). The runtime header stays opaque; the unit never sees JSRegPIC,
  JSObject or JSShape.

  R4: the monolith entry fill now consumes the backend's own
  definite-assignment list (b->regvm_fill) when it exists, and fills every
  register only when there is no analysis (NULL, e.g. a bytecode blob). The
  AOT_MUT_FILL_DROP_ALL macro drops the fill entirely for the negative control.

  get_global reads its atom from the live bytecode (qjs_aot_ld_u32 over the
  instruction operand) because atom ids are remapped at load time; the fused
  chain read tests both property-cache hits before writing either destination
  register.

Why we need it
  A step-per-op unit pays the interpreter's dispatch, operand decode and
  site-index loads on every op; that is why the P2/P3 unit was slower than the
  interpreter. Layer A removes those for the hot set and is the base the typed
  regions of P5 sit on.

What it adds
  quickjs.c
      always_inline fast-path helpers; qjs_aot_get_var_ref/load_this/
      move_xfer/unary/to_bool; qjs_aot_ld_u32-driven get_global; the
      b->regvm_fill entry fill; js_aot_gen_decode_insn records each operand's
      byte offset.
  quickjs-aot-gen.h
      JSAotGenInsn gains the per-operand offset table.
  quickjs-aot-rt.h
      qjs_aot_ld_u32 plus declarations for the new helpers.

  Nothing here is compiled without -DQJS_REGVM; QJS_AOT is off by default.
  Box2D checksum 546.1008391043414, test262-fast 50/81192, diff 398/0, ASan
  clean. The -DAOT_MUT_FILL_DROP_ALL build segfaults box2d (exit 139).

